  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history includes negative values (e.g., -0.25 or 0.50), indicating bearish sentiment.",
    "Reduce forecast magnitude by 5-10% if recent history shows a sharp spike followed by a drop (overshoot correction).",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is significantly above recent 5-day average, reduce by 10-15% to align with historical mean.",
    "Increase downward bias if true outcome consistently underperforms forecast (persistent underperformance), especially after high sentiment spikes.",
    "Avoid over-optimism in early forecast periods (e.g., first 5 days of 30d forecast) — apply a 5-10% downward adjustment if sentiment is neutral or negative.",
    "If sentiment history shows a gradual shift from neutral to positive (e.g., 0.00 → 0.50), slightly increase forecast but cap at 10% above recent 7-day average to avoid overcorrection."
  ]
}
